<title>FRANCE: Alcatel Alsthom Q1 sales up 12.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Alcatel Alsthom Q1 sales up 12.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter 1997.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover total				40,087    vs 35,774</p>
<p>     Telecom					15,179    vs 12,890</p>
<p>     Cables					  8,771    vs  8,744</p>
<p>     GEC Alsthom				   9,040    vs  8,478</p>
<p>     Systems					 6,756    vs  4,849</p>
<p>     Batteries				     1,086    vs  1,116</p>
<p>     Other and inter group sales		-745    vs   -303</p>
<p>NOTE - &quot;Alcatel Alsthom registered 1997 consolidated first quarter sales of 40.1 billion francs compared with 35.8 billion francs for the same period in 1996, representing a 12.1 percent increase,&quot; the company said in a statement. &quot;On a comparable basis, sales increased by 5.7 percent,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>&quot;1997 first quarter orders amounted to 42.4 billion francs compared with 43.6 billion for the first quarter of 1996. Orders decreased by 2.6 percent and on a comparable basis by 8.1 percent. This decrease was due to a drop in GEC Alsthom's contribution over the first quarter, wherein a significantly high level of orders were registered,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
